module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.witness_that_restates_the_answer

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data witness_that_restates_the_answer: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "witness_that_restates_the_answer" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a witness that restates the answer it claims to check** (INVALID STATE: an assertion is enrolled and greens, and is cited as coverage of a population or a fold, but the assertion is a COUNT OVER THE SAME FOLD that produced the population, or a MATCH WHOSE ARMS ALL RETURN THE SAME VALUE. The file compiles, the entry runs, the name of the claim is the property. Nothing independent was asked, so a wrong production still greens.",

    "THE TELL, AND IT IS THE WHOLE CLASS: `count(produced) == count(selected) + count(rejected) + count(unresolved)` where those three are partitions of the same coproduct the producer already exhausted; or `match standing { ArmA => true, ArmB => true, ArmC => true }`. Both are well-typed. Both can be named after a real obligation. Neither can go red unless the compiler itself is broken.",

    "THIS IS NOT CENSUS-LOCAL. A lens that asserts `count(findings) == count(scan(tree))` over the same scan, a floor witness that matches every `RequiredFloorDisposition` arm to `true`, and a census witness that joins a producer to its own partitions are the same class. The layer names the specimen, not the defect.",

    "HARM. DESIGN section 5: a typecheck and a grep are not consumers, and a merge-blocking test may not compare a live population to a number copied from the same tree. This class is that rule at assertion grain. The green is cited as coverage; the obligation it appears to discharge is the one that keeps flowing. DESIGN section 4b: a check whose RED is unauthorable is worse than absent, because it will be cited as coverage.",

    "SPECIMEN (2026-09-13, gunbc#11179, review 65482). `witness_rejected_and_unresolved_remain_visible` asserted `count(workload_census) == count(selected_workloads) + count(rejected_candidates) + count(unresolved_candidates)`. Those three lists are filters of one exhaustive `CandidateSelection` coproduct. Automating the literal collapses to `measure() == measure()`. The repair was an identity join over named subjects (`census_contains_subject`), not a count.",

    "DISTINCT FROM ITS NEIGHBOURS. Not `comparison_whose_operands_share_a_producer`: that class is a refusal-bearing comparison whose two operands share a producer. This class is an assertion that never asks a question -- there is no second operand, only a restatement. Not `discriminating_arm_built_but_never_enrolled`: there the discriminating input exists and is unconsumed; here the assertion is consumed and is tautological. Not `a_positive_control_certifies_the_defect_it_exists_to_catch`: there the control points at a wrong subject and still discriminates the accessor; here the assertion cannot discriminate any subject.",

    "THE CONTROL THAT ESTABLISHES A WITNESS IS A MUTATION OF AN INDEPENDENT INPUT. Flip a field the production does not itself mint, run the ENTRY, and require FAIL. gunbc#11179: setting `candidate_biome_blob_mismatch_control` observed `workflow_blob_sha_at_head` equal to the inspected blob turned `witness_blob_mismatch_is_refused_even_when_tests_ran` from PASS to `FAIL public_workload_census_witness_main` (local `claim_batch`, then reverted). A count-over-partitions assertion cannot be established that way, because there is no independent field to flip.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigation by review. The partition-count specimen was found by a reviewer, not by any executing check. Nothing in the substrate refuses a tautological `test fn`.",

    "CEILING: mechanically preventable. Whether every arm of a match returns the same constant, or whether both sides of a numeric equality are folds of one list, is decidable on the Node tree. It is not structurally impossible: a count equality can be a legitimate check when one side is a fixture or a versioned authority.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, CAPABILITY AND NOT ARTIFACT: a claim-admission analysis that refuses a `test fn` whose every match arm is the same constant, or whose equality operands are both derived from one producer in the same module, sufficient that a partition-count witness cannot enroll. A one-off mutation by an author on one fixture is the current state and is not this trigger.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
